Place autofill and password suggestions in the part of the page above the keyboard.

PopupBaseView measured the room below a field against
WebContents::GetContainerBounds(), the whole window. On a phone the
on-screen keyboard and the shell's dock cover its bottom, so suggestions
under a field low on the page opened under the keyboard instead of
flipping above the field. On OHOS the content area for placing the popup
ends where the page's visible viewport does (the view's insets,
setViewportInsets, take the keyboard off).

Only the popup's measure changes. Shrinking GetContainerBounds() itself
shrank the page too: its size is worked out from the container's.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-autofill-popup-above-keyboard.patch

